.TH "MIDIPORT.STATECHANGE_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MIDIPort.statechange_event \- MIDIPort: statechange event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]statechange\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]MIDIPort\f[R]
interface is fired when a port changes from open to closed, or closed to
open.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqstatechange\(dq, (event) => { })

onstatechange = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MIDIConnectionEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLE
In the following example the current \f[CR]MIDIPort.state\f[R] is logged
each time it changes.
.IP
.EX
port.onstatechange = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(port.state);
};
.EE
